%N A399636 Number of nonisomorphic connected right-Euclidean relations on n elements.
%C A399636 Each connected component has a unique nonempty reflexive equivalence class B; every nonreflexive vertex in that component has a nonempty out-neighborhood contained in B. For fixed |B| = k, isomorphism classes are counted by Burnside's lemma for the action of S_k on multisets of nonempty subsets of B.
%F A399636 Let H_k(x) = (1/k!)*Sum_{sigma in S_k} Product_{O} 1/(1-x^|O|), where O runs through the orbits of <sigma> acting on the nonempty subsets of {1,...,k}. Then Sum_{n>=1} a(n)*x^n = Sum_{k>=1} x^k*H_k(x).
%e A399636 For example, H_1(x) = 1/(1-x), H_2(x) = (1/2)*(1/(1-x)^3 + 1/((1-x)*(1-x^2))), and H_3(x) = (1/6)*(1/(1-x)^7 + 3/((1-x)^3*(1-x^2)^2) + 2/((1-x)*(1-x^3)^2)). Hence Sum_{k>=1} x^k*H_k(x) = x + 2*x^2 + 4*x^3 + 9*x^4 + 21*x^5 + 56*x^6 + ... .
%Y A399636 Cf. A001831 (labeled case).
